"note_claim": "The child's genes come from the sperm and egg that perform fertilization.",
"label": "SUPPORTS",
"quote": "During fertilization, when the egg and sperm join, the two sets of chromosomes come together. In this way, one half of a baby's genes come from the baby's mother and one half come from the baby's father.",
"reason": "The page explicitly describes fertilization as the process where genes from the mother and father combine, directly substantiating the note's claim about the source of a child's genetics."
}
